# Third-party code in vite-agent-inspect

This file carries the licence of every piece of code borrowed into this repository,
alongside the per-file provenance header that names it. The header format, the rules
for what may be borrowed, and the five borrows v0 expects are documented in
`docs/agents/provenance.md`.

## Entry format

Add one section per borrowing project, in the same commit as the file that borrows:

```
## <project>

Source:  <url>
Version: <tag, version or commit sha> (<date taken>)
Used in: <repo-relative path of each file that borrows>
Taken:   <what was taken, in a clause>

<the full, verbatim licence text>
```

Verbatim means verbatim, including the copyright line and its years. A summary, an
SPDX identifier alone, or a link is not a licence.

An icon set's entry carries one more line, `Kind:    icon set`, under `Source:`.
Icon artwork is credited once per set, not once per icon: a later icon from a set
already entered here needs only its file's provenance header, and its file named
under `Used in:` if it is a new file.

## Index

The five projects code is borrowed from, and the icon sets artwork is taken from, one
row per borrow, and the file that carries each borrow's provenance header.
vite-plugin-herdr lends two, in two files. Nothing else in this repository is
borrowed. `test/seam1/docs.test.ts` checks that every
provenance header has an entry here, that every file an entry names carries
that entry's header, and that this index agrees with the entries.

| borrow | from | licence | files |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| the fail-closed same-origin guard | vite-plugin-herdr | MIT | src/server/guard.ts |
| the payload draft the Pointer prose evolved from | vite-plugin-herdr | MIT | src/server/render.ts |
| the stack-frame parser | React DevTools | MIT | src/server/stack.ts |
| the deep element-at-point hit test | react-grab | MIT | src/overlay/deep-element.ts |
